From: David Griego <david.griego@foundries.io>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: qrb2210-arduino-imola: reserve M-05 boundary window

Workaround for 4 GB UNO Q boards (UNO Q M-05). The boot firmware lists
0x7b8ff000-0x7c9fefff (17 MiB) as System RAM. With the edk2 UEFI boot
chain, pages in this window raised synchronous external aborts during
OSTree deployment. Arduino's stock boot chain (the 251020 boot firmware
with U-Boot) still lists the window as System RAM. Reserve it with
no-map, keeping it out of the linear map and the page allocator, until
boot firmware with a fixed memory map is released.

Ported from the linux-arduino 7.0 version of this patch to linux-qcom
6.18, whose board device tree is qrb2210-arduino-imola.dts.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board firmware workaround; not for upstream]
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qrb2210-arduino-imola.dts | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qrb2210-arduino-imola.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qrb2210-arduino-imola.dts
@@ -563,3 +563,16 @@
 &xo_board {
 	clock-frequency = <38400000>;
 };
+
+&reserved_memory {
+	/*
+	 * UNO Q M-05 workaround for 4 GB boards: the boot firmware lists
+	 * 0x7b8ff000-0x7c9fefff as System RAM. With the edk2 UEFI, pages in
+	 * this window raised synchronous external aborts during OSTree
+	 * deployment. Keep the window out of the linear map and the allocator.
+	 */
+	m05_boundary_guard: m05-boundary-guard@7b8ff000 {
+		reg = <0x0 0x7b8ff000 0x0 0x1100000>;
+		no-map;
+	};
+};
